# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees with native to rel 1e-12 (abs floor 1e-10) in c_p[1], c_p[4], the press and c_virial and the forces; the reciprocal sum is 18.57 kcal/mol of c_p[4] (the first version without the native unscaled FFT was 1/N of it).
# oracle: pair amoeba permanent multipoles with the PME reciprocal sum (multipole_kspace: B-spline moments of order 5 on the 24x24x24 grid of pme-grid, the 3d FFT and the influence function, energy, forces, torques and virial) plus the real-space Ewald damping and self term, on the periodic AMOEBA water box (w119amoeba_box.data, boundary p p p, 216 waters) with ewald, ewald-alpha 0.4 (w119amoeba_ewald.key) and the multipole test parameters w119amoeba_mpole.prm; polarizabilities zero so the polarization terms are not compared (pe and c_p[5] are NaN natively).
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_box.data w119amoeba_mpole.prm w119amoeba_ewald.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 abs=1e-10 skip=pe,c_p[5]
units           real
boundary        p p p
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_box.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      amoeba exclude polar/kspace
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_mpole.prm w119amoeba_ewald.key
compute         p all pair amoeba
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
